<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver end down, off lows.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver end down, off lows.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and silver prices ended down on Friday but off opening lows in quiet trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said stronger world prices and improved local demand helped gold prices recover but the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) rose to 56,400 rupees per piece after opening at 56,100.  </p>
